Wait — check NewLossClearsPendingRecoverySignal sequence carefully with my planned implementation:

window 8, threshold 5. 10 losses → tier critical, pending false.
5 successes: window = 3 loss + 5 succ → 0.375 ≥0.3 → critical. At success #5: consecutive5 ≥5, tier_ (pre-recompute from success#4: window = 4 loss+4 succ = 0.5 → critical) ≠ healthy → set pending=true. Consume → true ✓.

Then 5 more successes (#6-10): window at #10 = last 8 = 2 loss + 6 succ → 0.25. Signal: at #6: consecutive=6 ≥5, tier_ pre-recompute = critical → SET pending=true AGAIN! Consume later would be true! Then EXPECT_FALSE(q.ConsumeRecoverySignal()) FAILS!

Hmm. Edge semantics problem: condition "consecutive >= threshold && tier != healthy" is a LEVEL condition, and setting happens every success while level holds. With bool assignment, once consumed, next success re-arms immediately while the level still holds. That's not "first satisfaction" edge.

True edge semantics: track previous condition state; set signal only on false→true transition:

```cpp
// in RecordSuccess after recompute:
const bool recovered_condition = consecutive_success_ >= config_.success_threshold &&
 tier_ != LinkHealthTier::kHealthy;
if (recovered_condition && !prev_recovered_condition_) pending = true;
prev_recovered_condition_ = recovered_condition;
```
