content.thinking:
A6 bug confirmed: `ReserveFacilityResource` calls `ReleaseResourcesForHolder(reservations, holder_id)` at line 101-103 BEFORE checking exclusive conflict at 104-111. So holder holding A, trying to reserve B held by someone else (exclusive) → A released, B fails → holder loses A (side effect on failure).

Also note the disabled check at line 96 happens BEFORE release — good (disabled fails without releasing). Wait: disabled check returns early at 96 before release — so disabled failure has no side effect already. Only the exclusive-conflict failure has the side-effect bug.

Fix: move `ReleaseResourcesForHolder` after the exclusive check (and after disabled check — already is).

But careful subtlety: if the holder already holds resource.id itself (existing->second.holder_id == holder_id), release_existing_for_holder releases it first, then re-reserve → fine. With reorder: exclusive check sees existing with same holder → not conflict → release (erase) → re-reserve → OK. But order matters: if we check conflict BEFORE release, holder-holding-itself case passes check (same holder), then release erases it, then re-insert. Fine.

New order:
1. disabled check (early return, no side effect)
2. exclusive conflict check (existing && holder != holder_id → fail, no side effect)
3. release_existing_for_holder
4. insert + success

